ut\": \"{\\\"claimant_name\\\": \\\"ama...\"}]\n\nThis confirms that the code does not require the entire fenced content to be valid JSON, contradicting the proposals' assumptions.\n\n#### Key Takeaway\nProposers should:\n1. Assume the code will **ignore non-JSON prose in fences** and score the last valid JSON object within them.\n2. Focus on testing the rule's handling of **invalid JSON** (e.g., floats, duplicate keys) and **fallback behavior** when no valid JSON exists in fences or top-level text.\n3. Avoid assuming that mixed JSON/prose in fences will invalidate the entire fenced content.",

